{{!-- A book citation, as controls rather than as text: "Book I, page 180" opens the GM's own
      copy of Book I at that page (module/books/rulebook-icons.js, openBookPage).

      ONE CHIP PER PAGE, which is what `bookPageCites` builds the list for: a move with a second
      printing reads "Book I, page 180, and again on page 300 for a site", and one control over
      that whole sentence would take a GM who pressed the words "page 300" to page 180.

      `sep` is printed BEFORE its chip and is empty on the first, so this loop never has to ask
      which chip it is on.

      A BUTTON, not a link. It is not a URL -- what it opens depends on what this world has been
      pointed at -- and a button is the element a keyboard already knows how to reach and press.
      Its styling (styles/stonetop.css) takes core's button chrome back off so it reads as the
      quiet run of text it replaced.

      Emitted on ONE line, because every one of the four places that draws this puts it inside a
      run of prose where a stray newline is a stray space. --}}
{{#each cites}}{{sep}}<button type="button" class="stonetop-book-cite" data-book="{{book}}" data-page="{{page}}" data-tooltip="{{tip}}">{{text}}</button>{{/each~}}
